<%# src/views/partials/guest-avatar.ejs — the single round guest avatar every
    surface that labels photos with a person's name renders: the Shared
    Gallery's By-person section head, the guest feed card header, and the
    admin Photos page's equivalents. Before this partial the same
    "photo-if-set, initials-if-not, clipped to a circle" markup was hand-copied
    per surface, and only two of the four ever showed the real photo — the
    divergence this closes off.

    The initials fallback derives from the shared app.locals.initials helper
    (src/utils/initials.js), never an inline one-liner, so every surface agrees
    on what "AF" means for a given name.

    Locals:
      avatarPath (required, nullable) — guests.avatar_path, the stored filename
                 only (rendered as /uploads/<avatarPath>). Null/empty renders
                 the initials fallback instead of a broken <img>.
      name       (required, nullable) — the guest's display name, used for the
                 initials fallback. A nameless guest falls back to "?".
      size       (optional) — 'md' (default, 34px: a section head) or
                 'sm' (28px: a feed card header, where the name line is
                 smaller). Any other value falls back to 'md'.

    Decorative by design: alt="" on the image and aria-hidden on the initials.
    Every call site renders the guest's name as real text immediately beside
    this, so announcing it here would make a screen reader say the name twice.

    loading="lazy" applies only to the 'sm' (feed-card) variant — a feed can
    render dozens of cards below the fold. The 'md' (section-head) variant
    sits in the first viewport (Shared Gallery / admin By-person heads), so it
    loads eagerly like the rest of that first paint. %>
<% var _size = (typeof size !== 'undefined' && size === 'sm') ? 'sm' : 'md'; %>
<% var _px = _size === 'sm' ? 28 : 34; %>
<span class="guest-avatar guest-avatar--<%= _size %>">
  <% if (avatarPath) { %>
    <%# The lazy attribute is emitted by a scriptlet branch, deliberately not
        by an escaping output tag: an escaped output tag turns the attribute's
        quotes into &#34; entities, which parse as a junk value and silently
        disable lazy loading rather than failing loudly. %>
    <img src="/uploads/<%= avatarPath %>" alt="" width="<%= _px %>" height="<%= _px %>"<% if (_size === 'sm') { %> loading="lazy"<% } %> decoding="async" />
  <% } else { %>
    <span aria-hidden="true"><%= initials(name) || '?' %></span>
  <% } %>
</span>
